    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22887" root="شكو and شكى" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَكِيَّةٌ</span></b>  an inf. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَكَا</span>. (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And also (TA)
a subst. signifying <i>A thing complained of</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْمٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِمَشْكُوٍّ</span>); like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمِيَّةٌ</span> a subst. signifying “ a thing
cast at or shot at ” (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْمٌ لِمَرْمِيٍّ</span>): (Msb, TA:) pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَكَايَا</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A remainder,</i> or <i>remaining portion,</i> (K and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شكى</span>,) of a
thing: mentioned by Sgh. (TA.)

